            "turn": 2,
            "text": "*Sets the brush down and tilts his head, studying the stranger's words.*\n\n\"English—I know not that tongue, nor have I heard it within these halls. If it is the speech of some far-off land, then say plainly what matter brings you before the king. What is it you wish to ask of me?\""
          },
          {
            "turn": 3,
            "text": "*Frowns slightly, then sets down the brush and leans forward with a look of plain curiosity.*\n\n\"Then we shall speak in this tongue of yours, though it sits strangely on my lips. A guest who cannot read our letters—this troubles me, for it is the very thing I have laboured over: a script the common folk might learn in ten days. Tell me, in your own country, how do the learned and the humble alike set down their words?\""
          },
          {
            "turn": 4,
            "text": "*Sets both hands on the low desk and considers the strange word with a faint, puzzled smile.*\n\n\"This 'weekend' I take to mean a day set apart from labour, and on such days I am happiest with the scholars of the Hall of Worthies, reading late into the night and arguing over books until my eyes grow dim. When the weather is clear I look in on the water clock or the sundial made with Jang Yeong-sil, and I confess a tender cut of meat at the evening meal pleases me greatly. In your country, how do folk spend their days of rest?\""
          }
        ]
